{
 "_what": "Capability sets and what a Codex agent launches with (#6419). internal/agent TestCodexSandboxRuleFixture holds TranslateToCodexPermissions and the launch flags to it; tests/frontend preset_enforcement.test.mjs holds preset_enforcement.js codexEnforced to it, so the form cannot say one thing while a launch does another. Written by hand from the rule, not by the code under test: change the rule, change this file, and both tests say where they disagree.",
 "_rule": "empty -> no flags (the CLI default). Capabilities never mean no sandbox (#6422): shell + file_read + file_write + git_write and no deny is the same as shell and no deny. The bypass flag comes only from the Bypass Permissions mode or a flag typed. shell and no deny -> workspace-write, never. shell with a deny -> workspace-write, on-request. file_read + file_write -> workspace-write, on-request. file_read -> read-only, on-request. web_access alone -> read-only, on-request. anything else -> workspace-write, on-request. web_access adds search. A shell:<pattern> is not shell. Other capabilities change nothing.",
